Firmware Baseline Manager

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs

Firmware Baseline Manager is an open-source, vendor-neutral authority for
facility-level firmware baseline policy and conformance state. It evaluates
observed and version evidence against published baselines and emits bounded
rollout and rollback eligibility decisions for external executors.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Firmware Baseline Manager does not collect or transmit any telemetry. All
state is written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the
machine running the software.

Firmware Baseline Manager accepts contributions from individuals and
organizations on the terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a
Contributor License Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution
guidance.
